Annex III
SUMMARY OF CONVEYANCES AND LARGE FREIGHT
CONTAINERS REQUIRED TO BE UNDER EXCLUSIVE USE
Conveyances and large freight containers are required to be under exclusive
use when loaded with any of the following:
(a) Unpackaged LSA‑I material, SCO‑I and SCO‑III (see para. 520);
(b) Liquid LSA‑I material in a Type IP‑1 package (see para. 521 and Table 5);
(c) Gaseous and/or liquid LSA‑II material in a Type IP‑2 package (see para. 521
and Table 5);
(d) LSA‑III material in a Type IP‑2 package (see para. 521 and Table 5);
(e) Packages, other than freight containers used as packaging, or overpacks
with an individual TI greater than 10 (see para. 526(a));
(f) Freight containers used as packaging with an individual TI greater than 50
(see para. 526(b));
(g) Packages or overpacks having the maximum dose rate at any point on the
external surfaces that exceeds 2 mSv/h (see para. 527);
(h) Packages, overpacks and freight containers with a total sum of TI exceeding
the values given in Table 10 (see para. 566(a));
(i) Packages, overpacks and freight containers with a total sum of CSI
exceeding the values given in Table 11 for “not under exclusive use” (see
paras 526(c), 566(c) and 569);

